From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:04:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: present deferred copy-path scanouts on compositor events

The Wayland copy path reads every flushed guest frame back into shared memory.
It used to commit as fast as the guest flushed and dropped a flush whenever the
compositor still held the next buffer; a repeating 30 ms timer (iceland gvm
0008/0011) then re-presented the dropped frame, waking the GPU worker about 33
times a second even while nothing on the guest screen changed.

Pace the copy path with wl_surface.frame callbacks instead: a flush that
arrives while the previous frame has not been drawn yet, or while the next
buffer is still held, only records the scanout's latest resource. The frame
callback or buffer release that makes it presentable wakes the worker through
the display fd, and process_display() presents the recorded frame. Nothing is
copied for frames the compositor would never show, and an unchanged guest
screen causes no wake-ups. CROSVM_GVM_REFRESH_MS remains a diagnostic that
re-presents every scanout periodically.

Co-Authored-By: gpt-6-astra <noreply@openai.com>

Purpose: Present deferred copy-path scanouts on compositor events.
Origin: https://github.com/yzddmr6/GunyahVM/commit/f0f00e83f005761be7772dd1d43ac597b3f0a77f
Upstream-Status: Downstream GunyahVM carry; not submitted to crosvm upstream.
